Z||000000||GodSend||06-25-2001||03:17 PM||||Hey there everyone,<P> Finally got around to searching for codes for my check engine light (I cleared all the codes last weekend, so these are all fresh).<BR>I recieved 2 codes, and went into further detail checking them out.  Here is what I found.<P>Code 32 - Egr Solenoid.  I have not checked the EGR yet, but I have removed the EGR tube and blocked off both the egr and other end.  Will this removal/blocking of the tube cause this 32 (it was a quick fix untill I can grab another tube).<P>Code 13 - o2 sensor.  I went to check the sensor and this is what I found<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/o2.jpg">  <P>It appears the wire going to the o2 sensor is completely missing (or is the actual sensor itself completely missing)?  Where does this wire come from (i want to see if I can find it, can't see it dangling around anywhere).  If I purchase a new sensor, will it come with the boot and everything (im looking at the picture of o2 senso in 6-6 of the haynes manual - it looks like I have alot missing).<P>Thanks guys<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by GodSend (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||BC-GT||06-25-2001||03:50 PM||||This is what a new one looks like installed. It comes with the male end wire, the female end should be hanging right behind the block somewhere, probably completely out of sight.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p43b965c80b52b13419a70029f479a599/fe631fb9.jpg.orig.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||06-25-2001||04:09 PM||||cant tell from the photos: V6 or 2.5L engine with missing wire?||||reg||1
Z||000003||GodSend||06-25-2001||04:21 PM||||2.8.. sorry guys.  So looking you picture bc-gt it looks like part of my o2 sensor is missing... well aint that some crazy stuff.. guess im off to crappy tire to see if they carry them... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||06-25-2001||04:45 PM||||the wire should go to a harness right about in the middle of the front of the engine - you can see it best from under the car, but you can get to it from the left side on the top.<P>  10:1 the wire is pulled out of the harness?!||||reg||1
Z||000005||GodSend||06-25-2001||07:12 PM||||I will have to look for the wire tomorrow.  The harness is not the one which goes through the firewall right? (are there any other wires coming out of this harness)... a # would be great so I know if I have found it.. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||GodSend||06-25-2001||09:16 PM||||Found the wire, with the other half of the o2 sensor.. still attached.. It had flown all the way over into the drivers side rear wheel well...(or pretty close)... <P>  I tried in vien to remove the o2 sensor from the downpipe.  I diden't have a #22 wrench, so I tryed really quickly with a pair of robogrips.. I did not try too hard because I did not want to strip the dam bolt.  I had hardly wany room to work with (from the top or underneath).  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/o22.jpg">  <P>I have circled the item which would make my life 10 times easier if I could remove it.  Is this piece removeable (I think it has to do with the break system, so I dont want to remove it and get air bubbles in the break fluid).  The bar has a line running from the bottom of it that dissapears into the wheel area)  Can anyone confirm this item?<P><BR>Thanks guys.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by GodSend (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||06-25-2001||10:19 PM||||That thing is your clutch slave cylinder. Yes you can remove it. A spring loaded rod will extend when you do, so when you go to put it back on just make sure that the rod fits into the recess in the clutch arm and squish it back into place. Don't undo the flex line going into the slave and you won't have any air bubble woes.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Indiana_resto_guy||06-25-2001||10:22 PM||||That's your clutch slave cylinder, you may disconnect it from the transmission by removing the 2 nuts-one on top and the other on the bottom. This should give you enough room so that when you get a bite on it you have the room to turn.||||reg||1
Z||000009||GodSend||06-26-2001||03:25 PM||||Thanks guys.  Got it out no problem.  Just went down to the local crappy tire and picked up a 22mm open ender... Cracked the nut and I could just removed it by hand after that.... put the new one in and brought the wrench back to get my cash back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Problem solved.||||reg||1
